// Expected verdict from J. Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models", PhD thesis, University of Edinburgh, 2008; checked here under sMRD.
// Load buffering where the write is the same on both branches.
//
// Source: Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models" (PhD thesis,
//         Edinburgh 2008), Figure 6.1, "reordering two instructions to one".
//
// r1 := x; if (r1 != 0) y := 1 else y := 1 has the traceset of r1 := x; y := 1,
// which may be reordered to y := 1; r1 := x. The thesis' framework allows the
// reordering, so r1 = r2 = 1 is ALLOWED -- as in sMRD, which lifts the two
// writes over the branch.
//
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  if (r1 != 0) {
    y := 1
  } else {
    y := 1
  }
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  x := r2
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) [sMRD]
